{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1269432-a-game-of-horror","id":1269432,"title":"A game of horror...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-20T21:03:53-08:00","id":1269432,"title":"A game of horror...","content":"Vampire: A game of personal horror<br /> Werewolf: A game of savage horror<br /> Mage: A game of.. uh... philosophical horror<br /> Wraith: A game of spiritual horror. Maybe a game of dead horror. Possibly a game of bureaucratic horror<br /> Changeling: A game of tripping balls on 'shrooms while watching Saturday morning cartoon horror.<br /> (Add you own)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T03:59:46-08:00","id":1269505,"title":"","content":"A Storytelling Game of ...<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> Personal Horror and The Beast Within<br /> Savage Horror and Spiritual Corruption<br /> Modern Magic and The Price of Power<br /> Private Passion and Life After Death<br /> Modern Fantasy and Loss of Innocence <br /> Medieval Horror and The War of Ages</div> <br /> At least that's how I've usually approached them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T07:45:45-08:00","id":1269562,"title":"","content":"I should have made this clear from the start - this humor, this is for jokes for people familiar enough with the games to make jokes about them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T08:59:27-08:00","id":1269583,"title":"","content":"Well. I never personally liked these &quot;xy horror&quot; misnomers. I think they are too restrictive and risks shoehorning the games into certain styles (glaring at you V5), while the games themselves grew up to contain much more.<br /> <br /> Also, I do think the WoD games contain horror to various degrees and styles, but I also always felt that labeling them as horror games is misplaced. They are dark urban fantasy games, with strong horror elements (though what gets how much focus varies by gameline),at least they came to be, relatively soon.<br /> <br /> I don't even think Vampire is a pure horror game and setting. It has too much power, too much stilization and, frankly, cool-faktor, on the characters' side (despite all the intentional oppressivenes of the setting - which I like) and at large in the setting too, to be that. But it has strong horror elements, yes.<br /> <br /> Mage, Werewolf, Changeling, Mummy are certainly not pure horror games, as the OP rightly presented and it's a struggle to shoehorn them into this.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there is a trend, for some time, to label everything &quot;dark&quot; as &quot;gothic&quot;, or &quot;goth&quot;, which annoys goths to no end (which I find exceedingly funny <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). Just like that, back then, there was a trend, to label everything that contained vampries and dark themes &quot;horror&quot;. Especially, since the urban fantasy genre wasn't around yet (and I have a fiemr oppinion that WoD indeed was one of its most important parents).<br /> <br /> <br /> So, that Aside, for me:<br /> <br /> Vampire: a game of gothic-punk nights and personnal horror. <br /> Werewolf: a game of raging for the dying world and of spirituality.<br /> Mage: a game of controversies (not that kind) and modern magick.<br /> Changeling: a game of innocence lost and powerful dreams.<br /> <br /> etc.<br /> <br /> Though, I admit, they aren't as short and catchy as the traditional ones.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}